# Deny everything, then allow back the few paths the image needs.
#
# This is an allow-list on purpose. A deny-list would have to be updated every
# time someone adds a directory, and this repo's working directories hold
# credential-grade material: `browser-profile/` is a LIVE corporate SSO session,
# `traces/` and `artifacts/` are Playwright traces and screenshots of the
# expense portal. Shipping any of them into a public GHCR layer would leak a
# signed-in session to anyone who can `docker pull`.
#
# Add a new entry below only if the running container genuinely needs the file.

*

!src/
!pyproject.toml
!requirements.txt
!README.md

# ...minus junk that rides along inside the allowed paths.
src/**/__pycache__/
src/**/*.py[cod]
src/**/*.egg-info/
